    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Asthma:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " only with an ICS, never as monotherapy; not for acute relief in an exacerbation. Dose 1–2 puffs every 12 h; synergistic with the ICS and permits a lower ICS dose."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Salmeterol (asthma, ≥ 4 y):"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " 1 inhalation twice daily with an ICS; EIB: 1 inhalation ≥ 30 min before exercise. No extra LABA for any reason."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Tremor, anxiety, tachycardia, mild temporary hypokalemia (same as SABAs). Using a long-acting agent as needed or more than twice daily raises arrhythmia risk."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": "Strong CYP3A4 inhibitors (ritonavir, ketoconazole): not recommended (cardiovascular effects). MAOIs/TCAs: extreme caution. Beta-blockers: may block the effect and cause severe bronchospasm. Non–K-sparing diuretics: hypokalemia/ECG changes may worsen."
     }
    ]
   },
   {
    "type": "paragraph",
    "attrs": {
     "indLeft": 18,
     "indRight": 0,
     "indFirst": -18,
     "spaceBefore": 0,
     "spaceAfter": 0,
     "line": null,
     "align": "left",
     "shade": null,
     "borders": null,
     "marker": {
      "text": "•",
      "font": null,
      "marks": [],
      "tabPt": 18
     }
    },
    "content": [
     {
      "type": "text",
      "marks": [
       {
        "type": "bold"
       }
      ],
      "text": "Overdose:"
     },
     {
      "type": "text",
      "text": " excess beta stimulation (seizures, angina, tachycardia up to 200/min, arrhythmias, hypokalemia, hyperglycemia, metabolic acidosis) and QTc prolongation with ventricular arrhythmias. Treat: stop the drug, symptomatic care, cardiac monitoring; a cardioselective beta-blocker may be considered judiciously."
     }
    ]
   }
  ]
 },
